In article <471c97fb.a590@mag.engin.umich.edu> news@caen.engin.umich.edu (CAEN Netnews) writes:

>  I feel that the kitchen sink should be eliminated. A new fountain/sink type should be created in it's place.I propose the culdron
>(*spelling may be wrong*)
I see no reason for this cauldron. Read further..

>  You could pour multiple potions into a culdron. This in turn would cause a mixing effect.  You could ignite a culdron with fire.
>This would boil the contents of the culdron. A player could add monster corpses to the mixture.
>Culdron recepies could be given by the oracle.
You can already mix potions. Try to #dip a potion into another one. But the
oracle surely should be able to give good recipes.
As for cooking of monsters in it, why should you bother? Just use the tinning
kit. Much simpler.

Other random thoughts..

When kicking doors with your boots on, you shouldn't get hurt.

Grenades were nice in some versions of 2.3 . Put them in again! But don't
call them grenades, call them potions of oil. When they hit something they
inflict fire damage to things beside them. This way they aren't quite as
powerful as the grenades were. (Of course you should have to light them first.)

Torches and new kinds of lamps. Forget about them! I proposed these additions,
but I don't think any longer that they would be useful. But perhaps you still
could fill lamps with potions of oil. This would add 2-4 'charges' to the 
lamp.

I LIKE GRID BUGS!
